  "about": "The field inventory declared for served provenance strings. These lists are declarations: tests/public-fields.test.mjs checks that they are consistent and that every declared name and id resolves on the served page, and nothing in this release scans served values against them. Every served provenance string lives in one of these fields, and each field is in exactly one class: locator (a web URL, a same-page anchor, a research document the annex publishes, or a file the site serves), prose (every token of a declared public kind), pointer (resolves by the rule named under pointers). The inventory was measured on the served data modules and the served evidence fixture; it covers every module at the top of the served directory and each fixture listed here. repositoryRoots: directory names (the repository's top level, its research subdirectories and the workspace's own) that make a slash-joined token a path wherever they appear in it (a path fragment is a locator, not words); fileExtensions do the same for a file name.",
